SM-T715 tablet: the first-run onboarding ships, adapted to the tablet.

Upstream's bin/omamobile-onboarding, dropped from this build until now, comes
in for the arm64 image, with the tablet's differences:
- The image ships the account with a placeholder password (0007's text names
  it); on the tablet it counts as no PIN, so the login nudge asks for setup
  and --inner makes the user choose a PIN or password (omamobile-set-pin
  --inner). has_pin tests it through unix_chkpwd exactly like the empty
  password: unix_chkpwd reads the candidate it checks from stdin
  NUL-terminated (a trailing newline would be part of the password; EOF
  without a NUL reads as an empty one), so the placeholder is sent with a
  NUL and nothing else, and never printed, logged or stored anywhere new.
- No fingerprint stack (/usr/lib/omamobile-fp absent): upstream already
  skips silently without its runner; test/onboarding-fingerprint.sh passes
  unchanged.
- The modem line is the tablet's, over shannond instead of the phone's
  omamobile-mobile-network: nothing when shannonctl is missing or does not
  answer within 10 s; "No SIM card." when the SIM is absent; when it is
  ready, the operator if shannond knows it (status --identifiers; a redacted
  one is not known) and that the APN is set in Réseau mobile (the app's
  name, t715-mobile-settings) from the app drawer; when the modem's own
  switch is off (t715-modem-power status --json), how to switch it on (the
  Modem tile). Every probe runs with LC_ALL=C and a timeout, as the tablet's
  other patches do.
- Golden's AI step, in --inner only, after the PIN and before the agent
  invitation, every choice optional and skippable: the AI desktop apps in one
  `gum choose --no-limit` (an app already installed is not offered,
  omarchy-pkg-present claude-desktop / openai-codex-desktop; they are
  downloaded from Omarchy's repository and need the network; a failed
  install says so and carries on), the language voice input uses
  ([whisper] language in ~/.config/voxtype/config.toml, shown as the
  language's own name for the ones the voice settings list, the code
  otherwise; nothing when Voxtype is not set up) with Setup > Voice changing
  it, and the default coding agent when none is set (omarchy-default-agent
  prints it, empty when none): one gum choose among Claude Code, Codex,
  OpenCode, Gemini, GitHub Copilot, Grok and Later; a choice runs
  omarchy-default-agent --install NAME, and Later falls back to upstream's
  invitation.
Tests: test/onboarding-mobile.sh follows the tablet's modem line;
test/onboarding-tablet.sh (new) covers the placeholder (nudge and --inner,
and the NUL-terminated candidate, read from the script rather than restated)
and the AI step; test/onboarding-identity.sh and
test/onboarding-fingerprint.sh pass as upstream's. Against omarchy-mobile
8991845 (omamobile-shell 0.2.147), after 0001-0014.

